---
import Shell from "../layouts/Shell.astro";
const notes = [
  {n:"01",type:"FIELD NOTE",date:"IN PROGRESS",title:"The personal starter",desc:"What belongs in a portfolio starter, what can be left out and why the first version should stay small."},
  {n:"02",type:"ENGINEERING",date:"IN PROGRESS",title:"Small systems, reliable software",desc:"Notes on making build pipelines, app architecture and everyday developer workflows less fragile."},
  {n:"03",type:"DESIGN NOTES",date:"IN PROGRESS",title:"Motion with a reason",desc:"A working collection of interaction patterns that clarify state instead of decorating the screen."}
];
---
<Shell title="Writing — Vinith Reddy Banda" description="Notes on engineering, design and learning in public.">
<section class="page-hero section-pad"><div class="section-index"><span>THE READING ROOM</span><span>NOTES / JOURNAL</span></div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-mark"></span> IDEAS, WRITTEN DOWN</p><h1 class="page-heading">Thinking<br/><em>out loud.</em></h1><p class="page-deck">Notes from the process: engineering decisions, design observations and lessons collected while building.</p></section>
<section class="writing-list section-pad"><div class="section-index"><span>THE INDEX</span><span>RECENT NOTES</span></div>{notes.map(n=><article class="writing-row"><div class="writing-meta"><span>{n.n} / {n.type}</span><small>{n.date}</small></div><div><h2>{n.title}</h2><p>{n.desc}</p></div><span class="writing-arrow">↗</span></article>)}</section>
<section class="writing-foot section-pad"><span class="micro-label">MORE NOTES, WHEN THEY’RE READY.</span><p>Writing is part of the work. This shelf will fill as the ideas become useful enough to share.</p></section>
</Shell>